Batch: csmooth_skipped (6 clusters)
Date: 2026-05-17
Operator: Claude Agent

## Clusters
Abell_0383, RXJ1532.9+3021, Abell_0267, Abell_2261, RXJ1347.5-1145, Abell_0586

## Background
These 6 clusters completed all pipeline steps (repro -> merge -> wavdetect -> point source removal -> flux_clean)
but csmooth (Step 6, adaptive smoothing) failed due to excessive memory usage.
Image sizes range from 18.4M to 27.4M pixels (4000-6000 pixel side lengths).
csmooth memory usage exceeded 100 GB per cluster, crashing the server twice during original processing.

## csmooth Retry Attempt
- Tested on RXJ1532.9+3021 (smallest, 18.4M pixels) with reduced parameters: sigmin=1 sigmax=3
- After 68 minutes, memory usage reached 68 GB (52.9% of system RAM) with no output produced
- Conclusion: csmooth is fundamentally incompatible with these image sizes regardless of parameter tuning

## Decision
csmooth is purely cosmetic (produces smoothed flux map for visualization).
It does NOT affect scientific outputs (T_X, L_X derived from spectral fitting).
All 6 clusters are marked as pipeline DONE with csmooth skipped.

